  "notes": [
    "The oracle is publicly available by immutable GHCR digest for linux/arm64; the tag is a discovery alias and is not an evidence identity.",
    "Fixed-theta evidence covers weighted offsets and diagonal, correlated, singular, and zero covariance factors under ML and REML.",
    "Optimized evidence covers one boundary random-slope walking-skeleton fit under both ML and REML.",
    "The public random-intercept API covers Dyestuff ML/REML fits and population/conditional prediction, including explicit new-group behavior and optimizer failure semantics.",
    "The public random-intercept API uses the owned block-Cholesky evaluator and returns the exact theta=0 boundary for Dyestuff2 under ML and REML.",
    "The public single-group API fits the correlated Sleepstudy intercept/slope model under ML and REML; ten Sleepstudy and eight synthetic fixed-theta slope cases verify block algebra before optimization.",
    "The public single-group API preserves two independent covariance terms sharing Subject for both explicit and numeric double-bar syntax; ten fixed-theta and two optimized Sleepstudy cases match pinned lme4 under ML and REML.",
    "A weighted-offset synthetic independent-slope case returns the exact zero slope-variance boundary under ML and REML.",
    "A shared model frame reproduces pinned subset-before-NA row selection, treatment and sum fixed-effect encodings, weights, additive formula/argument offsets, four ML/REML final fits, and known/new-group predictions.",
    "The general sparse backend preserves coupled random-intercept terms for nested Pastes and crossed Penicillin models across twelve fixed-theta cases, four final fits, and partial-new-group predictions.",
    "InstEval ML and REML exercise 73,421 observations and 4,100 random coefficients through the crossed sparse path with pinned objective, theta, beta, and sigma agreement.",
    "F02 reproduces the pinned non-LAPACK QR retained-column policy for exact and near aliases, empty interaction cells, and a threshold-sensitive full-rank case while retaining a coefficient-aligned null-space basis for contrasts and new-data prediction.",
